'''Mysterious Calamity''' (謎の厄災, ''Nazo no Yakusai'', '''Mysterious Calamity''') is a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy that appears in [[Anniversary/11th Year#Calamity in Doge Kingdom|Calamity in Doge Kingdom]]. It was added in [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Mysterious Calamity
|image = E 684.png
|first appearance = [[Anniversary/11th Year#Calamity in Doge Kingdom|Calamity in Doge Kingdom]]
|money drop = 11,115¢ - 43,904¢
}}

==Enemy==
The Mysterious Calamity is easily mistaken for a [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]], but doesn't behave anything like one. It has a slow attack rate and speed, weakens units hit for 8 seconds, strengthens by 100% at 33% HP, is immune to knockback and freeze, and attacks from 250 range by calling down meteors that hit units within an area of -800~800. While its stats are relatively low at first, this enemy becomes extremely strong in later stages of [[Anniversary/11th Year#Calamity in Doge Kingdom|Calamity in Doge Kingdom]], reaching up to '''3.5M''' HP and '''63k''' attack power in [[The Cats Allied]].

In all stages it appears in, the enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] which renders it impervious to damage until the Mysterious Calamity is defeated. In [[Decaying Town]] and The Cats Allied, the Base Barrier is not present until the base reaches 99% HP, which is when the Mysterious Calamity spawns.

==Strategy==
Rushing would be the ideal way to desecrate this offbrand [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] in earlier magnifications, as long as the player has access to [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]], and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]]. The latter of which would benefit immensely from [[Talents]].

In [[Age of Havoc]] and [[The Cats Allied]], however, stalling with Talented [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]] is almost necessary so you can chip it down with fast, high damage nukes, nukers like Fishman Cat and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]].

